# Bluenixx Build Manifest

Configure your git with your credentials.
example:

```
git config --global user.name "Your Name"
git config --global user.email "youremail@gmail.com"
```
Log in with your Google account on [Android Google Source](https://android.googlesource.com/) and copy the code that appears, paste it into the terminal, and then you can start your build.

Remember, all of this only applies if you're using your own build server. If it's local, there are more things to configure. Read the [Lineage OS](https://wiki.lineageos.org/) documentation.


Initialize the Repo:
```
repo init -u https://github.com/Bluenixx/bluenixx-manifest.git -b bluenixx-17.0 --git-lfs
```
Sync:
```
repo sync -c -j$(nproc --all) --force-sync --no-clone-bundle --no-tags
```

Then build Bluenixx:

```
source build/envsetup.sh
breakfast bangkk userdebug  # or: lunch bluenixx_bangkk-<release>-userdebug (run "lunch" to list choices)
mka bacon -j$(nproc --all)
```

### Thank you for choosing Bluenixx!
## Build flags

Set these environment variables before running `breakfast`:

| Variable | Values | Effect |
|---|---|---|
| `RELEASE_TYPE` | `OFFICIAL`, `NIGHTLY`, `SNAPSHOT`, `EXPERIMENTAL` | Build type. If unset (or invalid) the build is `UNOFFICIAL`. |
| `BLUENIXX_MAINTAINER` | maintainer username | Required for `OFFICIAL`. The `maintainer:product` pair must be listed in `vendor/lineage/bluenixx.maintainers`, otherwise the build falls back to `UNOFFICIAL`. |
| `WITH_GMS` | `true` | Includes GApps (MindTheGapps, `cinnamonbun` branch) and tags the zip as `GAPPS`. If unset the zip is `VANILLA`. |

Zip name:

```
bluenixx-17.0-<DATE>-<TYPE>-<GAPPS|VANILLA>-<device>.zip
```

Examples:

```
# Official, with GApps
export RELEASE_TYPE=OFFICIAL
export BLUENIXX_MAINTAINER=zedisspp
export WITH_GMS=true
breakfast bangkk
mka bacon -j$(nproc --all)

# Unofficial, vanilla
unset RELEASE_TYPE BLUENIXX_MAINTAINER WITH_GMS
breakfast bangkk
mka bacon -j$(nproc --all)
```

## Setting the flags in the device tree

Instead of `export`, the flags can be set with `:=` in `bluenixx_<device>.mk`:

```make
RELEASE_TYPE := OFFICIAL
BLUENIXX_MAINTAINER := zedisspp
WITH_GMS := true
INCLUDE_OVERMORROW := true
```

Notes:

- Put them **before** the first `inherit-product` line. `vendor/lineage` reads them when it is inherited, so anything set after that is ignored.
- A value set with `:=` overrides the terminal `export`. To keep it only as a default that the terminal can still override, use `?=` instead.
- `OFFICIAL` still requires the `maintainer:product` pair in `vendor/lineage/bluenixx.maintainers`.
